nt millions of public  dollars to raise cattle and sheep the  ranch manager has had multiple  confrontations with his neighbors he  knew nothing about sheep bogler says his  men have been threatened his equipment  vandalized his water rights challenged  more recently he was charged with  trespassing his sheep on grazing land  he's used for decades you're looking  pretty silly the blm offered to let him  off the hook if he pled guilty but  bogler saw that as a trap and is  fighting back in court against an  opponent with deep pockets of public  money every court motion costs vogler  thousands of dollars mere chump change  to the other guys i just paid a law bill  for last month it's 15 thousand bucks  for one lawyer i now have two  i mean and they're just dragging me down  by my  guts until i go broke bogler doesn't  think government should be in business  competing against smaller private owners  he and his neighbors further argue that  federal statutes are clear no government  entity can have federal grazing permits  but snwa does i'm the fifth generation  another nevada rancher kenna glockner  whose family has lived on the same  lincoln county land since the 1860s says  she's hanging on by her fingernails  because the snwa ranch commandeered the  rangeland assigned to her herds for more  than half a century just took it over  she hired lawyers and won a costly  battle then snwa started a federal  appeals process that will freeze her out  of her range for a decade or more an  expensive process the snwa can afford  but she cannot why are they overrunning  everyone why are they having all these  complaints and battles  and the only  solution i mean the only answer we can  we can come up with is  is that were in their way maybe they  want you to react with violence  absolutely then they can  see what kind of people we have to deal  with  well  i am not the brightest bulb in the  drawer but i am not the  dimmest bulb either  don't try and gaslight me snwa is a  government body competing against  private enterprise we previously asked  how they can graze livestock on public  land when federal regulations state that  government agencies are barred from  getting grazing permits snwa says their  lawyers advise them that they can snwa  declined to comment about vogler's  allegations because they say the matter  is in the courts george knapp 8 news now
 

